## Decision
The check-and-replace of the session secret is wrapped in a file lock. This makes the operation atomic across concurrent `serve` processes or workers. Without the lock, two processes could both see a stale secret and each write a different replacement, leaving sessions inconsistent. The design choice is documented in ADR 0003, now marked accepted.

